PATCH: zephyr_mbedtls_session_tickets_ungate — make session tickets available under TLS 1.2
============================================================================================

Written against: Zephyr 4.5.0-dev  (commit fbfc5f19636d07f214b3f573fa9b673a58e7e932)
Target platform: any   (this is a pure Kconfig fix — no per-arch impact)
Application:     /workspace/projects/hello_eink  (LLSS e-ink client, TLS 1.2 pinned)

SUMMARY
-------
In `modules/mbedtls/Kconfig.mbedtls` at the pinned commit, the symbol
`MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS` is defined inside an `if MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3
... endif` block:

    if MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3

    config MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS
        bool "Support for RFC 5077 session tickets in TLS 1.3"

    config MBEDTLS_SSL_EARLY_DATA
        bool "TLS 1.3 early data (0-RTT) support"
        depends on MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS
        ...

    config MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS1_3_COMPATIBILITY_MODE
        ...

    endif # MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3

Two things are wrong about this:

  1. **RFC 5077 is the TLS 1.2 session-ticket RFC.**  The prompt string even
     says "RFC 5077 session tickets in TLS 1.3", but RFC 5077 was published
     in 2008 for TLS 1.2.  TLS 1.3 tickets are RFC 8446 §4.6.1.  Upstream
     conflated the two.

  2. **The if-guard makes the symbol invisible when TLS 1.2 is the only
     enabled protocol.**  Any `CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS=y` in
     prj.conf is then silently dropped (no warning) because Kconfig hides
     unsettable symbols.  Without the macro, the mbedTLS client neither
     advertises the session-ticket extension nor processes incoming
     NewSessionTicket messages — session resumption falls back to the
     legacy session-ID mechanism, which most modern multi-frontend servers
     (Traefik, sharded nginx, anything fronting Let's Encrypt) do not
     honour.  The Zephyr `NET_SOCKETS_TLS_SESSION_CACHE_PERSISTENT` layer
     still serialises whatever session struct exists, but on reconnect the
     client offers only a session ID, so the persisted state is useless
     against servers that require tickets.

WHY WE NEED THIS LOCALLY
------------------------
`hello_eink` pins to TLS 1.2 (see the "TLS 1.3 KILL SWITCH" block in
`prj.conf`) because TLS 1.3's NewSessionTicket is sent *after* the handshake
completes and current Zephyr does not catch it for the persistent cache —
breaking cross-boot resume.  Under TLS 1.2, the NewSessionTicket rides
inside the handshake itself and the persistent cache picks it up correctly,
*provided* `MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS` is actually defined in the build.
This patch makes that possible.

WHAT THE PATCH DOES
-------------------
Moves `MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS` out of `if MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3`,
gives it an explicit `depends on MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2 ||
MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3`, and updates the prompt/help text.  Leaves
`MBEDTLS_SSL_EARLY_DATA` and `MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS1_3_COMPATIBILITY_MODE`
inside the if-block — both genuinely are TLS 1.3 only.  EARLY_DATA's
`depends on MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS` continues to work across the
moved scope.

PORTING / UPSTREAM NOTES
------------------------
Right fix is upstream.  If Zephyr later moves SSL_SESSION_TICKETS out of
the TLS 1.3 if-block (or fully rewrites this section), this patch will fail
to apply — drop it and remove `CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS=y` from
prj.conf only if the upstream symbol is still visible under 1.2.

The patch is reversible: `apply_patches` in `workspace/scripts/zephyr-project.sh`
detects already-applied state via `git apply --check --reverse` and skips,
so re-running `zephyr-project.sh build` is idempotent.

IMPACT IF DROPPED
-----------------
Build still succeeds.  TLS 1.2 handshakes still work.  But session
resumption falls back to session-ID only — first connect per boot is a
full ~3 s handshake, cross-boot persistence is effectively a no-op against
ticket-only servers.

---

--- a/modules/mbedtls/Kconfig.mbedtls
+++ b/modules/mbedtls/Kconfig.mbedtls
@@ -59,10 +59,22 @@
 	select PSA_WANT_ALG_HKDF_EXTRACT
 	select PSA_WANT_ALG_HKDF_EXPAND
 
+# --- hello_eink patch: SSL_SESSION_TICKETS visible under TLS 1.2 too ----------
+# Upstream (commit fbfc5f19636d) places this symbol inside `if TLS1_3` even
+# though RFC 5077 session tickets are fundamentally a TLS 1.2 mechanism.
+# Ungate it so 1.2-only builds can actually request and persist tickets.
+# See workspace/projects/hello_eink/patches/zephyr_mbedtls_session_tickets_ungate.patch
+config MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS
+	bool "Support for RFC 5077 (TLS 1.2) / RFC 8446 (TLS 1.3) session tickets"
+	depends on MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_2 || MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3
+	help
+	  Enable client/server handling of session-ticket-based resumption.
+	  TLS 1.2: NewSessionTicket arrives inside the handshake (RFC 5077).
+	  TLS 1.3: NewSessionTicket arrives post-handshake (RFC 8446 §4.6.1).
+# --- end hello_eink patch -----------------------------------------------------
+
 if MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3
 
-config MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS
-	bool "Support for RFC 5077 session tickets in TLS 1.3"
 
 config MBEDTLS_SSL_EARLY_DATA
 	bool "TLS 1.3 early data (0-RTT) support"
